<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marananta</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">4th century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marananta was a Buddhist monk, said to have come from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a> or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, who brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a> to Baekje from the Eastern Jin dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. According to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samguk-sagi">Samguk sagi</a> he arrived in 384 and was received by King Chimnyu, who soon built a temple for him. Buddhism became the faith of the Baekje court and later spread from Baekje to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>.</p></div>
